Solving 5 ^ (2 * x) - 9 * 5 ^ x - 10 = 0 for x

Tidying to 5 ^ (2 * x) + -9 * 5 ^ x = 10

Rewriting equation in terms of 5 ^ x
gives (5 ^ x) ^ 2 + -9 * 5 ^ x = 10

Substituting   x1 for 5 ^ x gives
 -9 * x1 + x1 ^ 2 = 10

Using quadratic equation formula

Solutions are x1 = 10 and x1 = -1

Applying substitution 
    x1 = 5 ^ x

   to    : 
    x1 = 10 # x1 = -1

   gives : 
    5 ^ x = 10 # 5 ^ x = -1



Solving disjunct 5 ^ x = 10

    x = log(5, 10)
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct 5 ^ x = -1

5^x = -1 has no real roots, 5^x must be > 0

